      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The influence of acute controlled normovolemic hemodilution on the parameters of central hemodynamics was studied in 40 patients with obliterating diseases of lower extremities with eukinetic, hyperkinetic and hypokinetic types of blood circulation. Cardiac output was found to increase and general peripheral resistance to decrease after hemodilution. The greatest changes were noted in patients with the initial hypodynamic type of blood circulation. It was found that 24% increase of the oxygen transport function of the blood circulation was reached without an increase of the intensity of cardiac activity and hypoxia of the myocardium."},
